    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0209" n="1667" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p2/pg1667"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">110.11/5–1551: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hong Kong</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McConaughy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hong Kong</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-05-15T16:00:00+09:00">May 15, 1951—4 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3376. To Acheson for Under Secretary Matthews.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d87-f1"/>
                    Additional possibility makes it desirable for Marshall and Chase to postpone
                    departure until May 23.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d87-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McConaughy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d87-f1" n="1" xml:id="d87-f1-content">
                <p>The telegram was circulated to Nolting, Nitze, and Merchant.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d87-f2" n="2" xml:id="d87-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 3850 to Hong Kong, May 18, 1951, informed Marshall and Chase that their
                    plan to remain in Hong Kong until May 23 was approved (110.11/5–1851).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
